#
# The build context is the repo root (server/docker-compose.yml sets
# `context: ..`), and server/Dockerfile does `COPY server/ ./server/`. Two
# reasons this file has to exist:
#
# 1. SECURITY. server/data holds putzii-server.conf — the AES state key and
#    the token hashes, 0600 — plus the encrypted plan. Without this line a
#    build on the deploy host copies all of it into the image layer.
# 2. It makes the build WORK at all. The runbook chowns server/data to
#    10001:10001 before building (the container runs as that uid), after
#    which the build daemon, running as the deploy user, cannot read the
#    directory and the build fails with "error from sender: open
#    .../server/data: permission denied".
#
# Keep this narrow: invariant 7 cross-checks that every APP_SHELL asset
# appears in the Dockerfile's COPY block, so excluding an app file here would
# break the image while the guard still reads green.
server/data/
.git/
.github/
